rossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2007, 11]]}, "DOI": "10.1109/wiiatw.2007.4427637", "type": "proceedings-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2008, 1, 14]], "date-time": "2008-01-14T20:03:30Z", "timestamp": 1200341010000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Training Intelligent Agents in the Semantic Web Era: The Golf Advisor Agent"], "prefix": "10.1109", "author": [{"given": "Ioannis N.", "family": "Athanasiadis", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "263", "event": {"name": "2007 IEEE/WIC/ACM International Conferences on Web Intelligence and Intelligent Agent Technology - Workshops", "location": "Silicon Valley, CA, USA", "start": {"date-parts": [[2007, 11, 5]]}, "end": {"date-parts": [[2007, 11, 12]]}}, "container-title": ["2007 IEEE/WIC/ACM International Conferences on Web Intelligence and Intelligent Agent Technology - Workshops"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2020, 10, 14]], "date-time": "2020-10-14T15:39:36Z", "timestamp": 1602689976000}, "score": 23.317545, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/4427637"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2007, 11]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1109/wiiatw.2007.4427637", "published": {"date-parts": [[2007, 11]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 10]], "date-time": "2026-06-10T16:10:28Z", "timestamp": 1781107828600, "version": "3.54.1"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "IGI Global", "isbn-type": [{"value": "9781599041087", "type": "print"}, {"value": "9781599041100", "type": "electronic"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2007]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Multi-agent systems (MAS) advocate an agent-based approach to software engineering based on decomposing problems in terms of decentralized, autonomous agents that can engage in flexible, high-level interactions. This chapter introduces scalable fault tolerant agent grooming environment (SAGE), a second-generation Foundation for Intelligent Physical Agents (FIPA)-compliant multi-agent system developed at NIIT-Comtec, which provides an environment for creating distributed, intelligent, and autonomous entities that are encapsulated as agents. The chapter focuses on the highlight of SAGE, which is its decentralized fault-tolerant architecture that can be used to develop applications in a number of areas such as e-health, e-government, and e-science. In addition, SAGE architecture provides tools for runtime agent management, directory facilitation, monitoring, and editing messages exchange between agents. SAGE also provides a built-in mechanism to program agent behavior and their capabilities with the help of its autonomous agent architecture, which is the other major highlight of this chapter. The authors believe that the market for agent-based applications is growing rapidly, and SAGE can play a crucial role for future intelligent applications development.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.4018/978-1-59904-108-7.ch008", "type": "book-chapter", "created": {"date-parts": [[2011, 5, 24]], "date-time": "2011-05-24T11:39:40Z", "timestamp": 1306237180000}, "page": "143-172", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Scalable Fault Tolerant Agent Grooming Environment (SAGE)"], "prefix": "10.4018", "author": [{"given": "H. Farooq", "family": "Ahmad", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "Communication Technologies, Japan"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Hiroki", "family": "Suguri", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "NUST Institute of Information Technology, Pakistan"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "2432", "container-title": ["Architectural Design of Multi-Agent Systems"], "link": [{"URL": "https://www.igi-global.com/viewtitle.aspx?TitleId=5177", "content-type": "unspecified", "conte